                <pb facs="0449" n="361" sameAs="frus:frus1933v04/pg361"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">724.3415/3336: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Paraguay</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Horn</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Asunción</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1933-09-29T18:00:00-04:00">September 29, 1933—6
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received September 30—3:02 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>94. My 93, September 29, 10 a.m. I have just had presented to me the following
                    reply from the Minister of Foreign Affairs: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“The Paraguayan Government cordially thanks the American Government for
                            its friendly interest in the satisfactory solution of the Chaco conflict
                            and has the satisfaction of informing it that it has accepted without
                            reservations the proposal of the mediators acting under mandate of the
                            League.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Horn</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
